WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.160
From Hannibal's tastiest meal preps&nbsp;
to Slippin' Jimmy's messiest exploits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.960
these shows are proof that some TV prequels are&nbsp;
even better than the stories they came from.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:17.220
A prequel to a reboot, Caprica hit screens in&nbsp;
2010, a year after the dramatic ending of science&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.680
fiction drama Battlestar Galactica. Battlestar had&nbsp;
been a relaunch of a short-lived sci-fi adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:28.740
from 1978, with producer Ronald D. Moore turning&nbsp;
the campy family adventure into a gritty war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:34.380
story that dazzled audiences with dark, sobering&nbsp;
storylines and unpredictable twists and turns.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:40.260
Caprica was entirely different: a sci-fi political&nbsp;
thriller set decades earlier on a thriving world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:46.380
where A.I. technology is in its infancy. Taking&nbsp;
place nearly 60 years before the Earth/Cylon war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:52.680
of BSG, the show explored the relationship between&nbsp;
two rival families, the Graystones and the Adamas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.460
and saw the advent of the technology&nbsp;
that would lead to the Cylon race.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:03.000
"I'm Zoe. And the avatar. And the robot. Like&nbsp;
some kind of whatchacallit three-parter."

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.720
"Trinity."

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.440
Starring Eric Stoltz and Esai Morales as family&nbsp;
patriarchs Daniel Graystone and Joseph Adama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.740
respectively, the series set itself apart from BSG&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.640
with a focus on political and religious&nbsp;
intrigue and profound personal drama.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.920
"What would you do if you had the&nbsp;
chance to be with your daughter again?"

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.340
Packed with social allegory, Caprica garnered rave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.680
reviews from critics. The&nbsp;
Guardian called the series:

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.240
"Dense and intelligent sci-fi [...]&nbsp;
complex, bizarre and ambitious."

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.900
Despite the acclaim, Caprica&nbsp;
lasted just a single season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.300
but it's remained a cult favorite ever since.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.480
A Batman prequel arrived in 2014&nbsp;
in the form of Gotham, a grim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.380
hard-boiled crime series set in the&nbsp;
city Batman would one day protect.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.760
"Bruce. My name is Bruce Wayne."

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:00.180
In it, Bruce Wayne is a young boy, so the series&nbsp;
focuses more on Gotham PD Lieutenant James Gordon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.320
played by Ben McKenzie, and his efforts&nbsp;
to combat the city's criminal underworld.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.580
The series opened with the killing of&nbsp;
Gotham socialites Thomas and Martha Wayne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.740
As the show progressed, audiences met&nbsp;
many of Batman's eventual rogues' gallery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:18.480
with future villains the Penguin, Catwoman,&nbsp;
the Riddler, and the Joker making appearances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.860
as well as several new baddies like&nbsp;
Jada Pinkett Smith as Fish Mooney.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.080
"Only my friends call me Fish."

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:33.540
Praised for its slick production and stylish&nbsp;
storytelling, Gotham ran for five seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.640
ending with a now-adult Bruce Wayne donning&nbsp;
cape and cowl to become the Dark Knight.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.100
The Big Bang Theory was a multi-camera&nbsp;
sitcom about three geeky friends in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.880
Pasadena who fill their days with&nbsp;
video games, comic books, and RPGs.
 &nbsp;

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:52.080
"It's just some quantum mechanics with a&nbsp;
little string theory doodling around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.340
edges. That part there? That's just a joke. It's&nbsp;
a spoof of the Bourne-Oppenheimer approximation."

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:03.060
A smash hit for 12 astonishing seasons, Big&nbsp;
Bang became a franchise in 2017 with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.980
debut of prequel series Young Sheldon, about&nbsp;
the awkward youth of child prodigy Sheldon.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.720
Young actor Iain Armitage plays Sheldon,&nbsp;
whose trials and tribulations include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.180
skipping four grades. This makes him a&nbsp;
social misfit and yet, occasionally, a hero

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.880
"Him being so young isn't like weird?"

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.380
"I'm basically fifty."

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.300
"And we're basically 12, so it all works out."

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.240
Balancing a tough school&nbsp;
schedule with problems at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.080
he also has to deal with the frustrations&nbsp;
of having a dimmer-witted older brother.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.840
"Morning. I slept in the nude last&nbsp;
night. Felt every little breeze."

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.560
A heartfelt and heartwarming family sitcom&nbsp;
that brings a fresh angle to the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.020
with stories about Sheldon's social struggles,&nbsp;
Young Sheldon was a big hit, with IndieWire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:54.300
calling out its strong mix of comedy and drama and&nbsp;
its empathetic approach to the central character.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:01.380
Perry Mason began in the 1930s as a series of&nbsp;
novels by Erle Stanley Gardner before becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.320
a series of films, a radio drama, and eventually&nbsp;
a hit TV series starring Raymond Burr that ran for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:14.220
nearly 300 episodes beginning in 1957. Revived&nbsp;
briefly in the 1970s as The New Perry Mason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.140
Burr returned to the role for a series of&nbsp;
TV movies all the way through the 1990s.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.820
"No further questions."

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:25.560
After a decades-long absence, the&nbsp;
unflappable lawyer reappeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.340
the 2020 prequel series Perry&nbsp;
Mason, starring Matthew Rhys.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.580
"You were in the war, weren't you?&nbsp;
The way you hold your cigarette,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.410
hiding the ember in your palm."

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.840
"I guess I'm still trying not to&nbsp;
give them something to shoot at."

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:41.460
The series takes place years before Mason&nbsp;
becomes a lawyer. In this darker drama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:46.140
Mason is a beleaguered private investigator&nbsp;
whose business is struggling during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.280
Great Depression. The series' first season&nbsp;
tells a single story across eight episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:53.520
as Mason investigates a grisly child murder case.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.540
The show's strongest asset&nbsp;
might be its phenomenal cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:02.760
which includes Tatiana Maslany and John&nbsp;
Lithgow, among many other standouts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:08.520
Praised for its sophisticated story, compelling&nbsp;
mystery, evocative style, and overall panache,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.800
Perry Mason built off decades of previous&nbsp;
stories to provide a new spin on an old classic.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:19.920
Born from the mind of Muppets creator Jim&nbsp;
Henson, The Dark Crystal was an iconic '80s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:25.200
family fantasy film full of ancient relics&nbsp;
and mystical powers. It became an enduring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.940
cult classic thanks to its incredible design,&nbsp;
captivating story, and blend of light-hearted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.800
playfulness with a foreboding sense of doom.&nbsp;
Though there was talk of a sequel for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.420
a prequel eventually materialized: The&nbsp;
Dark Crystal: The Age of Resistance.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:45.840
Released in 2019 as a Netflix original, the series&nbsp;
was helmed by action director Louis Leterrier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.880
and boasted an all-star cast voicing its&nbsp;
ensemble of puppet actors, including Mark Hamill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:55.260
Taron Egerton, Awkwafina, Jason&nbsp;
Isaacs, and Helena Bonham Carter.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:58.380
"These are the world's greatest&nbsp;
puppeteers working with Louis Leterrier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.140
a brilliant director. It's a look&nbsp;
that you've never seen before."

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:03.060
Set long before the events of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:07.440
Age of Resistance sees a group of childlike&nbsp;
Gelflings on a journey to unite their people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.460
to fight back against the devious and&nbsp;
tyrannical Skeksis that rule them.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.880
The series delivered a powerful&nbsp;
story of friendship, loyalty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:20.640
and indomitable spirit. Gorgeously produced with&nbsp;
sumptuous visuals and a story that expanded on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.260
Henson's original. The Dark Crystal: Age&nbsp;
of Resistance was a magical treat that did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:29.880
more than justice to a classic, making for&nbsp;
a stellar fantasy series in its own right.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:35.340
Director Peter Jackson's groundbreaking&nbsp;
Lord of the Rings trilogy brought J.R.R.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.860
Tolkien's fantasy world to the mainstream in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:43.200
early 2000s. Expertly realized with a lavish&nbsp;
production budget, it quickly became iconic.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:51.300
"Always remember, Frodo. The ring is trying to&nbsp;
get back to its master. It wants to be found."

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:56.460
Following a trilogy of prequels adapted from The&nbsp;
Hobbit, many wondered where the franchise would go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:02.100
next, but it would be a decade before Amazon's&nbsp;
Rings of Power prequel series landed in 2022.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:07.260
Rings of Power is set in the Second Age of Middle&nbsp;
Earth, long before the events of Lord of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:13.980
Rings, yet includes several crossover characters,&nbsp;
notably immortal elves Elrond and Galadriel. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:19.980
new evil rises in the East, the different races —&nbsp;
Dwarves, Elves, Hobbits, and Man — prepare to rise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:25.560
up and meet it head-on. The series is a visual&nbsp;
treat, a true spectacle that brings the cinematic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:30.420
experience to the small screen. Story-wise,&nbsp;
it expands upon themes from Jackson's trilogy.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.180
Strong performances, an intriguing plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:37.980
and plenty of surprises have helped it garner&nbsp;
critical acclaim, too, with Variety calling it:

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.660
"A perfectly winning adaptation that&nbsp;
unfolds swashbuckling adventures with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.840
clear reverence and affection for&nbsp;
the considerable mythos behind it."

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:50.880
A massive success for the streaming giant, it's&nbsp;
anyone's guess where the series will go following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:55.560
its debut season, but it's already proven&nbsp;
itself a worthy addition to Tolkien's world.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:01.560
In 2001, the comedy troupe known as "The&nbsp;
State" produced an offbeat comedy film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:05.640
Wet Hot American Summer, that followed&nbsp;
the antics of a group of teen counselors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:10.020
at a 1980s summer camp. Members of "The&nbsp;
State" were joined by a remarkable cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:15.180
including young Paul Rudd, Bradley Cooper,&nbsp;
and Amy Poehler alongside veterans David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:19.980
Hyde Pierce, Molly Shannon, and Janeane&nbsp;
Garofalo. Though it flopped in theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:25.860
its surreal humor and raunchy tone made it a&nbsp;
cult classic. More than a decade later in 2015,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:30.900
a prequel series arrived on Netflix, Wet&nbsp;
Hot American Summer: First Day of Camp.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:37.260
The entire cast — now 15 years older — returned,&nbsp;
still playing teenagers in a story set several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:42.480
months before the film, on the first day of&nbsp;
camp in 1981. Even Rudd, Cooper, and Poehler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:46.500
who had since achieved megastardom,&nbsp;
came back for the eight-episode series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:50.400
with the likes of Kristin Wiig and&nbsp;
Jason Schwartzman joining them.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:56.400
Lauded by critics for its wild, off-the-wall&nbsp;
comedy, the show became a big hit for Netflix. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.980
2017, it was followed by a sequel series,&nbsp;
Wet Hot American Summer: Ten Years Later.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.200
Alfred Hitchcock's Psycho was&nbsp;
a seminal 1960s thriller that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:11.940
almost single handedly gave rise to the&nbsp;
modern psychological horror genre. Psycho&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:15.480
centers on a young woman who winds&nbsp;
up in a hotel run by Norman Bates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:20.100
a twisted madman whose obsession with&nbsp;
his own mother turns him into a killer.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.680
"Well, a boy's best friend is his mother."

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:28.800
A Hollywood classic and box-office smash, it was&nbsp;
followed by a few lesser sequels and a TV movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:35.220
called Bates Motel in 1987. In 2013, when the&nbsp;
title was repurposed for a prequel television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:40.020
series starring Freddie Highmore as a young&nbsp;
Norman, no one had particularly high hopes.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:45.660
The series introduces a teenaged Norman,&nbsp;
whose mother Norma, played by Vera Farmiga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.980
purchases a motel after the death of her&nbsp;
husband. Trouble strikes when Norma is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:54.420
forced to kill an attacker, leading to a&nbsp;
series of cover-ups and conspiracies that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:58.980
threaten to expose them both. Surrounded&nbsp;
by violence, Norman's fragile mental state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:04.080
deteriorates. As he slowly spirals into madness,&nbsp;
his mother struggles to deal with his condition.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.700
Bates Motel is a riveting psychological&nbsp;
thriller that ran for five seasons.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:11.760
"You told her something happens&nbsp;
to me when I black out. You said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.480
I change. That I'm not myself. Who am&nbsp;
I, Mother? Who am I and what do I do?"

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:19.740
The final season was a jaw-dropping&nbsp;
remake of the original film. The Los&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:24.720
Angeles Times called the series "twisty,&nbsp;
mood[y] [and] modern." Bates Motel is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.920
blueprint for how to craft a clever,&nbsp;
fresh prequel to an iconic property.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:33.600
The 1991 film Silence of the&nbsp;
Lambs brought author Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.180
Harris' novel to the big screen with aplomb.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.680
"Oh, Clarice, your problem is you&nbsp;
need to get more fun out of life."

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:46.680
Star Anthony Hopkins gave a spine-chilling — and&nbsp;
Oscar-winning — performance as sociopathic serial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:50.700
killer Hannibal Lecter. Technically,&nbsp;
this was Lecter's second big-screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:55.440
appearance. He originally featured in&nbsp;
Michael Mann's 1986 flick Manhunter.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:01.740
Danish actor Mads Mikkelsen took on the role&nbsp;
for a 2013 NBC prequel series titled Hannibal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:06.360
which chronicled the years before Lecter was&nbsp;
imprisoned for a series of cannibalistic murders.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:12.000
Drawing mostly on material from Harris' novel&nbsp;
Red Dragon, the show saw renowned psychiatrist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.760
Lecter assisting intrepid FBI agent Will Graham,&nbsp;
played by Hugh Dancy, as a criminal profiler.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:21.240
"Not fond of eye contact, are you?"

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:25.140
"Eyes are distracting. See&nbsp;
too much. Don't see enough."

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.220
Created by Bryan Fuller, the series&nbsp;
reimagined the relationship between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:33.780
the two future adversaries, as Lecter —&nbsp;
whose murderous inclinations are explored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:37.020
in secret — becomes obsessed&nbsp;
with the young FBI agent.

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:38.940
"It seems you have an admirer."

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.900
"You think someone sent me in&nbsp;
here because they admire me?"

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.720
Dark, disturbing, and bold, Hannibal pushed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.440
boundaries of network censorship and&nbsp;
was rewarded with universal acclaim.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:55.680
Star Trek had done prequels before, with the&nbsp;
2001 series Enterprise set in the early days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.680 --> 00:12:01.980
of Starfleet. 2017's Star Trek: Discovery also&nbsp;
takes place in the past, just a decade before Kirk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:07.800
and Spock. In that show's second season, we meet&nbsp;
Captain Pike and the U.S.S. Enterprise. In 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:13.200
their story spun off into its own series: Star&nbsp;
Trek: Strange New Worlds. Starring Anson Mount,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:18.600
Ethan Peck, and Rebecca Romijn as classic&nbsp;
characters Pike, Mr. Spock, and Number One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:22.920
it explored early missions of the Enterprise&nbsp;
that had only previously been hinted at.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:26.940
Joined by a mix of returning&nbsp;
franchise icons like Uhura –

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.500
"Oh, can I help?"

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:32.280
"No."

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:39.180
– Nurse Chapel, and Dr. M'Benga, plus new&nbsp;
characters La'an Noonien Singh, Ensign Ortegas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:45.360
and Andorian engineer Hemmer, the series was a&nbsp;
retro return to sci-fi adventure. While Star Trek:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:50.160
Discovery and Star Trek: Picard focused on&nbsp;
darker, more adult-themed serialized stories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:55.500
Strange New Worlds successfully recaptured&nbsp;
the classic Trek spirit with family-friendly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.620
episodic stories that took the&nbsp;
crew to new worlds each week.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:02.880
With a strong cast and a big budget,&nbsp;
the series refreshed the final frontier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:07.560
Strange New Worlds was hailed as a return to&nbsp;
form with a stirring mix of big adventure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.620
thought-provoking science&nbsp;
fiction, humor, and heart.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:16.320
Creating a spin-off of an acclaimed series&nbsp;
can be risky. No matter how good it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:20.700
it may always live in the shadow of its&nbsp;
parent series. Such was the predicament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:26.340
when the 16-time Emmy Award-winning Breaking&nbsp;
Bad announced that supporting star Bob Odenkirk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:30.660
would lead spin-off series, Better Call&nbsp;
Saul. The fact that it would be a prequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.680
and would run alongside the final seasons&nbsp;
of Breaking Bad, made it even trickier.

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:37.860
"Did you just bring a bomb into a hospital?"

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.920
"What? Was I supposed to leave it on his car?"

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:45.720
But Odenkirk and series creator Vince&nbsp;
Gilligan pulled off the impossible.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.160
"What the hell do you think you're doing?"

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.660
"I need Saul. I need him right now."

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:55.920
The show, which debuted in 2015, explored more of&nbsp;
unscrupulous lawyer Saul Goodman's shady past and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.920 --> 00:14:01.260
underhanded dealings, while appearances from&nbsp;
Giancarlo Esposito as Gus Fring and Jonathan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:06.120
Banks as Mike Ehrmantraut helped flesh out&nbsp;
the Breaking Bad universe by enriching old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:10.920
stories with new context. In time, the events&nbsp;
of the series caught up with its predecessor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:14.940
which even allowed for the brief return&nbsp;
of Bryan Cranston as Walter White.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:18.780
With a more left-of-center vibe&nbsp;
and a colorful cast of quirky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:23.340
eccentric characters, Better Call Saul was&nbsp;
a series with its own identity while still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:28.320
delivering gut-wrenching, nail-biting crime&nbsp;
stories. Standing on the shoulders of a giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:33.240
the series may have soared even higher, with&nbsp;
The Guardian declaring it even more profound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:36.840
and outstripping Gilligan's&nbsp;
former series in nearly every way.

